{\footer }{\header \pard\ql\li0\ri0\f0\fs20\cf0 AI Item Generation for the Big Five Personality Traits\par}\pgwsxn12242\pghsxn15842\pard\li0\ri0\f0\fs20\cf0 Study Name: (Online) AI Item Generation for the Big Five Personality TraitsResearchers:Cathy (Xijuan) Zhang, Assistant Professor. Office location: 367 Behavioural Science (BSB), Keele Campus.Email: Xijuan@yorku.ca.Purpose of the Research:The purpose of this research is to evaluate how large language models generate psychological items in the Expanded format to measure the Big Five Personality traits. The resulting data and code will be used to publish findings in peer-reviewed outlets, present results at academic conferences, share anonymized datasets and scripts in an open repository, and develop practical guidelines for AI-based scale development.What You Will Be Asked to Do in the Research:\u160?You will complete an online survey assessing the Big Five personality traits, followed by criterion measures on the Big Five traits. The criterion measures include\u160? 1) Short Dark Triad Test; 2) Behaviour Report Form; 3) Psychopathology; 4) an item about volunteerism; 5) an item about cultural activities; 6) Nerdy Personality Attributes Scale; 7) Nonverbal Immediacy scale; 8) Big Five Mini-Marker test.The survey ends with demographic questions. The survey is expected to take approximately 15 minutes to complete.Risks and Discomforts:Some of the questions on the survey may cause some minor psychological discomfort. If you feel too uncomfortable during the study, you can immediately withdraw without penalty. If you have any questions about the study, feel free to contact us via email at yorkzhangquantlab@gmail.com. If you feel uncomfortable, the following mental health services can be reached:- Student Counselling service: https://students.yorku.ca/counselling-\u160? Good2Talk-a free 24/7 service for online mental health resources: https://good2talk.ca/-\u160? Suicide prevention and Crisis response helpline: https://988.ca/\u160?Benefits of the Research and Benefits to You:The benefits of this research include potential insight into your social anxiety level. In addition to earning a 0.25 URPP credit, your participation will provide insight and experience into the inner workings of a psychological study and an opportunity to be a part of research that will aid the scholarly community. The findings of this research will increase our understanding of how we can leverage AI to improve measurement in psychology.Voluntary Participation and Withdrawal:Your participation in the study is completely voluntary and you may choose to stop participating at any time. Your decision not to volunteer, to stop participating, or to refuse to answer particular questions will not influence the nature of your relationship with York University either now, or in the future. If you stop participating, you will still be eligible to receive a URPP credit for agreeing to be in the project, even if you withdraw without completion of the research.\u160?Due to the anonymous nature of this study, it is important to note that once you have submitted your responses, it will not be possible to identify and remove your specific data from the dataset should you wish to withdraw from the study. This is because we do not collect any personally identifiable information that would allow us to link your responses back to you.If you decide to withdraw from the study, you can do so at any time during the survey by simply closing your browser window without submitting your responses. In this case, your partial data will not be saved or used in the study. However, once you have completed the survey and submitted your responses, we will not be able to remove your specific data from the dataset. We encourage you to carefully consider your participation before submitting your responses. If you have any concerns, please feel free to ask questions before proceeding with the study.Confidentiality: \u160?All information you supply during the research will be held in confidence, and your name will not appear in any report or publication of the research.Your data will be collected through QuestionPro, a company not affiliated with York University and with its own privacy and security policies. There is always a risk during web-based transmission that data may be intercepted by a third party (e.g., government agencies, hackers), and thus confidentiality and privacy cannot be guaranteed. You can review QuestionPro\u8217?s privacy policy here: [https://www.questionpro.com/help/privacy-policy.html].The raw data will be downloaded and safely stored on the lab's laptops, which are also password-protected, and only research staff/research team members will have access to this information. The raw data will be cleaned up for data analysis, which may involve re-labelling or re-organizing questionnaire items and removing data from participants who withdraw from the study. To maintain transparency and promote open-science principles, we intend to publish the cleaned data on the Open Science Framework (OSF) or GitHub following the publication of our research paper; the OSF or GitHub will retain the cleaned data indefinitely. The published dataset will be anonymous, with all personal information that could potentially identify participants excluded, as we do not collect any information that could identify participants. Confidentiality will be provided to the fullest extent possible by law.Questions About the Research?\u160? If you have questions about the research in general or about your role in the study, please feel free to contact Dr. Cathy (Xijuan) Zhang by email (yorkzhangquantlab@gmail.com). This research has received ethics review and approval by the Human Participants Review Sub-Committee, York University\u8217?s Ethics Review Board and conforms to the standards of the Canadian Tri-Council Research Ethics guidelines. If you have any questions about this process, or about your rights as a participant in the study, please contact the Manager, Research Ethics in the Office of Research Ethics, York University (e-mail ore@yorku.ca). This office oversees the ethical conduct of research studies and is not part of the study team. Everything that you discuss will be kept confidential.\par\pard\li0\ri0\f0\fs20\cf0 \par \par \par\pard\li0\ri0\f0\fs20\cf0 By selecting \u8220?I agree to participate\u8221?, you are consenting to participate in the \u8220?(Online) AI Item Generation for the Big Five Personality Traits\u8221? conducted by Dr. Cathy (Xijuan) Zhang. By consenting, you have understood the nature of this project and wish to participate. You are not waiving any of your legal rights by consenting to participate.\par\pard\ql\fi0\li400\ri0\fs20\ls1{{\listtext\pard\f0\fi0\li400\ri0 1.\tab}\f0\fs20\cf0 I agree to participate.\par
